{
  "id": "T-LEAVE3",
  "title": "T-35 / T-10 (a): leaving a merged company settles money in the right order - a client leaves 3 (1/3 vs 2/3, the leaver never takes the company balance, still right after a save/reload), the host leaves 3, a 2-member leave (half each), and a ban's 'remove everything' takes an offline member out with no payout",
  "preconditions": "Fixture save1 (host melaus/Prabaha, client Client1/REX) plus role d (Client2, joins as a NEW player - charconfirm armed before hostload), as T-P1-3. Build with HostMemberLeave (T-35/T-10) deployed. ONE mid-run host save into the rig's own save copy (fixture_reset re-prepares it before every run). The ban leg bans Client2 and unbans it again; ends dissolved with Client2 dropped. Exact thirds are not computable by the rig (derive adds constants only): leg A asserts leaver > 0, leaver != whole, remaining > leaver, every remaining member = the host ledger; the readout checks the SPLIT line's figures.",
  "instances": 3,
  "vars": {
    "clientPid": "Client1",
    "hostPid": "melaus",
    "dPid": "Client2",
    "session": "save1"
  },
  "oracles_absent": [
    "NullReferenceException",
    "\\[Merger\\] accept .* REFUSED",
    "upload SKIPPED",
    "\\[Forfeit\\] remove property .* REFUSED",
    "\\[Wallet\\] apply:"
  ],
  "oracles_report": [
    "\\[EconProbe\\] wallet",
    "\\[Merger\\] '.+' left their merger group",
    "\\[MPSave\\] merged share"
  ],
